# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings.
#
# The Windows build environment is MSYS2 (see docs/hardware.md): its bash and
# zsh both fail on CRLF with `$'\r': command not found`, which looks like a
# corrupt script rather than a line-ending problem. Git's core.autocrlf=true --
# a common global setting on Windows -- rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, so
# a fresh clone breaks build.sh and flash.sh before they ever run. Pin them.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
env.sh          text eol=lf

# The host scripts are invoked directly via their shebang on macOS/Linux.
*.py            text eol=lf

# LaunchAgent templates are consumed by macOS launchd.
*.plist.in      text eol=lf

# Firmware/asset binaries and build artifacts: never touched.
*.bin           binary
*.png           binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary

# deps.lock is parsed line-by-line by setup.sh: a CRLF blank line reads as
# "\r", not "", so the comment/blank skip misses it and it tries to clone "".
deps.lock       text eol=lf
